From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH local 006] panvk/csf: PANVK_KBASE_SAFE_SUBMIT A/B switch

Adds an opt-in conservative mode (env PANVK_KBASE_SAFE_SUBMIT=1) that
restores the serialization the aggressive kbase submit/recycling paths
removed: per-job 0x233 cache flush, no ring-drain completion shortcut,
graphics drain before tiler-heap replacement, and inline heap TERM.
Used to attribute GPU faults between the submit path and the heap
recycling path; default off, behaviour unchanged.

Generated-by: LLM

